<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:dev="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:beh="clr-namespace:Harp.Behavior;assembly=Harp.Behavior"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:spk="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Spinnaker;assembly=Bonsai.Spinnaker"
                 xmlns:orc="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:orv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Video;assembly=OpenRigs.Video"
                 xmlns:ext="clr-namespace:UclOpenCoenBehaviourBox;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:mf="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Manifest;assembly=OpenRigs.Manifest"
                 xmlns:hd="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.HarpDevices;assembly=OpenRigs.HarpDevices"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="Binning" DisplayName="Binning" Description="Camera binning, 1 for full resolution, in place of rig.yml's. Stays set for later runs until cleared. Blank: rig.yml's camera binning." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
        <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" />
        <Property Name="SessionId" />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl): SubjectId and SessionId from this node's properties or the command line (--property:SubjectId=...), the run length (whole minutes) and the camera's exposure and gain (CameraExposureUs and CameraGainDb, taken live by the camera, Hardware &gt; CameraLiveControls) as parameters the controller may change until Go, and the control endpoint the rig agent talks to (TCP 5561). The workflow starts into ready mode: board connected, camera armed and streaming, nothing recorded, waiting for Go. At Go the IDs and the run length are checked once and published as RunSettings, which logging waits for; if an ID is empty or the run length is not 1 to 9999, the workflow stops with "Sequence contains no elements." and nothing is recorded. Stop from the controller ends the workflow through ExperimentStoppedException, closing every file.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId />
              <SessionId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>RunLengthMinutes</Name>
                  <Value>30</Value>
                  <Description>How long to record, in whole minutes (1 to 9999).</Description>
                  <Minimum>1</Minimum>
                  <Maximum>9999</Maximum>
                  <WholeNumber>true</WholeNumber>
                </Parameter>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>CameraExposureUs</Name>
                  <Value />
                  <Description>Camera exposure in microseconds, taken by the camera live until Go. Starts at rig.yml's; at most the trigger period less 1,000 (19,000 at 50 Hz).</Description>
                  <Minimum>100</Minimum>
                </Parameter>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>CameraGainDb</Name>
                  <Value />
                  <Description>Camera gain in dB, 0 to 5, taken by the camera live until Go. Starts at rig.yml's.</Description>
                  <Minimum>0</Minimum>
                  <Maximum>5</Maximum>
                </Parameter>
              </Parameters>
              <Commands />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SubjectId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SessionId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterValue">
                <orcl:Name>RunLengthMinutes</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Name>RunLengthToInt</scr:Name>
              <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(it)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>RunSettingsValid</Name>
              <Description>Subject and session given, and the run length from 1 to 9999 minutes.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Item1.Trim().Length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; Item2.Trim().Length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; Item3 &gt;= 1 &amp;&amp; Item3 &lt;= 9999</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:First" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RunSettings</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="9" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogLabExperiment.bonsai" />
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Hardware</Name>
        <Description>The box's devices as lib-open-rigs pieces, each from its own entry in rig.yml (ReadLabRig's RigConfigs) and logging itself once the experiment folder exists: ReadyGate (Ready once the board's clock is set and the camera has sent a frame: ReadyWaitsFor), the Behavior board BehaviorBoard-Main, its clock (ClockFromBoard: the board's Harp clock set to UTC, re-sent each heartbeat until it agrees), the running wheel on encoder port 2 (WheelDistanceCm), the camera Camera-Overhead (Binning, a launch property, in place of rig.yml's while set) on the board's camera trigger (CameraTriggers: started once the camera acquires), CameraExposureUs and CameraGainDb taken live by the camera (CameraLiveControls), and the editor's preview (Preview).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Binning" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadyGate.bonsai">
              <ReadyWaitsFor>HarpClockSet, Camera-Overhead</ReadyWaitsFor>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.BehaviorBoard.bonsai">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
              <CommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</CommandsSubjectName>
              <DataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</DataSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.ClockFromBoard.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.RunningWheel.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
              <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
              <WheelDistanceSubjectName>WheelDistanceCm</WheelDistanceSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:SpinnakerCamera.bonsai">
              <Name>Camera-Overhead</Name>
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
              <DataSubjectName>Camera-Overhead.Data</DataSubjectName>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:CameraTriggers.bonsai">
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
              <BoardCommandsSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</BoardCommandsSubjectName>
              <BoardDataSubjectName>BehaviorBoard-Main.Data</BoardDataSubjectName>
              <CamerasExpected>Camera-Overhead</CamerasExpected>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:CameraLiveControls.bonsai">
              <Camera>Camera-Overhead</Camera>
              <ExposureParameter>CameraExposureUs</ExposureParameter>
              <GainParameter>CameraGainDb</GainParameter>
              <Board>BehaviorBoard-Main</Board>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>Preview</Name>
              <Description>The editor's preview window (config\main.layout): Value.Image and SampleInterval take 5 images a second from Camera-Overhead.Data, from Start, so it shows the camera in ready mode, and the last three nodes show beside it the exposure and gain the camera reports for its frames (CameraSettings).</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Overhead.Data</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>Value.Image</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SampleInterval">
                      <rx:Interval>PT0.2S</rx:Interval>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>Camera-Overhead.Data</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SampleInterval">
                      <rx:Interval>PT0.2S</rx:Interval>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Name>CameraSettings</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Description>The exposure and gain the camera reports for its frames (chunk data), 5 a second, for the editor's readout window (config\main.layout): what the camera took, not what was asked for.</scr:Description>
                    <scr:Expression>"Exposure " + Value.ChunkData.ExposureTime.ToString("F0") + " us   Gain " + Value.ChunkData.Gain.ToString("F2") + " dB"</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Logging</Name>
        <Description>What the box adds to the experiment folder (LogLabExperiment, before Hardware, makes it at Go with BonsaiData_Async, Settings_Rig and Settings_Experiment; the board and camera log themselves): RecordVideo counts the run, LogControlEvents adds the controller's events to BonsaiData_Async, RecordHarpDevices checks the board at Start and writes its record and register map, and ExperimentManifest records the experiment, completed when the run's frames are in.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Camera-Overhead.Data</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>RecordVideo</Name>
              <Description>The run: subscribed only once PathPrefix exists (Take reads its Count at subscription), it takes the run length's worth of frames (RunLengthToFrames) and then completes, which completes the manifest's run and reports Finished. The camera piece records the video and its CSV itself, every frame from its first until the workflow stops.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
                    <Name>RunLengthToFrames</Name>
                    <Description>Frames to record: run length (minutes) x 60 x the camera trigger frequency of BehaviorBoard-Main in rig.yml.</Description>
                    <Workflow>
                      <Nodes>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>RunSettings</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                          <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main</Name>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                          <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                          <scr:Name>RunLengthToFrames</scr:Name>
                          <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(Convert.ToDouble(Item1.Item3) * 60.0 * Item2.Settings.CameraTriggerController.Trigger0Frequency)</scr:Expression>
                        </Expression>
                        <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                      </Nodes>
                      <Edges>
                        <Edge From="0" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source2" />
                        <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                        <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                      </Edges>
                    </Workflow>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Count" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                    <rx:Count>3000</rx:Count>
                  </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogControlEvents.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="hd:RecordHarpDevices">
              <Name>RecordHarpDevices</Name>
              <Description>Checks the Behavior board at Start and records it into each experiment, from rig.yml alone (OpenRigs.HarpDevices): for each Harp device in rig.yml whose data this workflow publishes (BehaviorBoard-Main.Data), the board on its portName must have its usbSerial, or the workflow stops saying which board is where; 0.5 s after the experiment folder (PathPrefix) appears it asks the board for a register dump on BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands, which the board&apos;s log records (Go comes long after HarpClockSet, so the dump is on the UTC clock); and it writes BehaviorBoard-Main\BehaviorBoard-Main_device.json (WhoAmI, hardware, firmware and core versions, Harp and USB serials) and BehaviorBoard-Main\BehaviorBoard-Main.yml, Harp.Behavior&apos;s register map (the Open Rigs logging spec, section 5). A board reporting another WhoAmI stops the workflow. ExperimentManifest expects both files (harp in its ExpectedFiles).</Description>
              <hd:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</hd:ConfigRoot>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="mf:ExperimentManifest">
              <Name>ExperimentManifest</Name>
              <Description>Writes manifest.json into the experiment folder (OpenRigs.Manifest), finding PathPrefix itself: once when the folder appears (outcome running) and again when the run ends. Its input is the run, the frames recorded: completed when the run length&apos;s frames are written, error with a Watchdog&apos;s message, run.items the frame count; a controller stop is stopped, with the stop&apos;s reason. It records the machine, this repo&apos;s commit, Bonsai&apos;s command line (--property values), who launched it and sent Go (the parameters at Go are in Settings_Experiment), rig.yml&apos;s path and hash as read at Start (its settings are in Settings_Rig), and what the experiment must leave: a folder for each device in rig.yml this workflow publishes (BehaviorBoard-Main/, Camera-Overhead/), Settings/Settings_Rig_ and Settings/Settings_Experiment_, each settings file expected on its own, and (harp) for each Harp device in rig.yml the two files RecordHarpDevices writes, BehaviorBoard-Main_device.json and BehaviorBoard-Main.yml, which the overnight copy (jacuzzi-ingest&apos;s ingest-rig) alarms on if missing. A device folder holding only those two counts as empty. Errors on the board&apos;s logging chain do not reach it.</Description>
              <mf:IngestScript>coen-behaviour-box</mf:IngestScript>
              <mf:ExpectedFiles>auto;harp;Settings/Settings_Rig_;Settings/Settings_Experiment_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_Async_</mf:ExpectedFiles>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Count" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Finished</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="ConfigRoot" />
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="5" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every device in this machine's rig.yml that the workflow publishes, over ZeroMQ, for the live view (OpenRigs.LiveView, StreamDevices): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558, on every interface, from Start (in ready mode too). Camera-Overhead.Data as Camera-Overhead.video, 5 JPEG frames a second at 320 x 240; BehaviorBoard-Main.Data as BehaviorBoard-Main.encoder, the raw count from AnalogData, 10 a second; each rate and size can be changed in rig.yml under the device's liveView:. Also elapsed, seconds since the experiment folder (PathPrefix) appeared, once a second, and every 5 s liveview: this workflow, its commit, and the devices streamed and skipped and why. Every message carries RigId, the machine's name, and the session key: "ready" until the experiment folder exists, then its name, sub-&lt;SubjectId&gt;/ses-&lt;SessionId&gt;_&lt;start&gt;. Its ConfigRoot is the workflow's, as RigConfig's, RecordHarpDevices' and Logging &gt; RecordVideo's are, so --property:ConfigRoot moves all four. Last in the workflow, because it streams only subjects built before it. A port already in use (another workflow streaming) stops the workflow at Start with NetMQ's AddressAlreadyInUseException, before the camera is triggered.</Description>
        <lv:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</lv:ConfigRoot>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="ConfigRoot" Description="The root under which each machine has its own configuration directory, &lt;ConfigRoot&gt;\&lt;MACHINE-NAME&gt;\rig.yml, read by ReadLabRig (which publishes it to the camera's video writer), RecordHarpDevices and LiveView." />
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="8" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="8" To="6" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="8" To="7" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
